Project Charter
Project Name
Payment Block & Debit Balance Reduction and Governance Program
Background
As of 27 July, ICECO continues to carry significant balances in both Payment Blocks and Vendor Debit Balances, creating risks related to supplier relationships, working capital visibility, financial reporting accuracy, and operational efficiency.
Current Position
Payment Blocks
Total Payment Block Balance: $232.3M
Key contributing categories:
Supplier Factoring: $139.3M
Price/Quantity Discrepancies: $43.4M
Non-PO / 2-Way Match: $23.7M
Manual Blocks: $6.7M
Master Data issues: $5.7M
Debit Balances
Total Debit Balance: $5.67M
Approximate supplier count: 2,367 items
Concentrated across EMEA, China, NAM, and LATAM suppliers with aged unresolved balances.
Business Problem Statement
Unresolved payment blocks and vendor debit balances are impacting:
Timely supplier payments
Working capital transparency
Financial statement accuracy
AP operational productivity
Vendor relationship management
Internal and external audit compliance
A structured governance model is required to drive sustainable reduction and prevent future recurrence.
Project Objective
Payment Block
Reduce payment block inventory by addressing root causes and establishing preventive controls.
Debit Balance
Reduce vendor debit balances through recovery, clearing, offsetting, and process correction initiatives.
